WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 20 Student Video
Unit 5, Lesson 4: Apostles

1
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.100
Have you

2
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:26.380
ever heard the argument that the apostles of Jesus all died brutal deaths, being

3
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:31.380
stabbed to death, skinned alive, crucified, and therefore they didn't make up the

4
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.160
resurrection, and Christianity must be true?

5
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.800
I heard an argument quite similar to this growing up and found it quite compelling.

6
00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:44.320
But recently I decided to dig deeper and examine the historical evidence that the

7
00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:47.220
apostles actually died as martyrs.

8
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.340
What I found was not only surprising, but quite powerful.

9
00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:55.620
Here are five key points of what I found.

10
00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:56.360
The

11
00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:06.820
first point to understand is what is meant by an apostle.

12
00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:12.080
When we look at the beginning chapters of Acts, we see that the disciples are coming

13
00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.220
up with a replacement because of Judas who had betrayed Jesus.

14
00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:18.660
And there's two criteria that they utilize.

15
00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:24.840
One, the replacement had to have been with Jesus since his baptism by John the

16
00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:30.220
Baptist. And second, the replacement to be in the twelve had to be an eyewitness of

17
00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:36.200
the risen Jesus. The second point is to understand that the earliest message that

18
00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:40.560
the Apostles preached was that Jesus had risen from the grave.

19
00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:45.520
From the letters of Paul to the book of Acts where we see the first Christians going

20
00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:49.780
out and building the church, the message that they gave was always tied

21
00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:55.580
to the resurrection. There is no early Christianity apart from the belief that Jesus

22
00:01:55.580 --> 00:02:01.500
rose from the grave. The third point is that the apostles preached a message

23
00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:05.100
in direct opposition to the Roman state.

24
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:10.500
When the apostles stood up and said that Jesus is God, they were essentially saying

25
00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:16.320
that Caesar is not. they were proclaiming that a criminal against the Roman state

26
00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:22.000
was the risen Lord. They preached a message that made them enemies of the Roman

27
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:22.300
state.

28
00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:28.940
And the fourth point is that the Apostles would not stop preaching the risen Jesus

29
00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:32.880
even when they were threatened, beaten and thrown in prison.

30
00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:36.660
If you look at the beginning of the book of Acts they're told by the religious

31
00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:41.460
leaders just stop proclaiming that Jesus is Lord and will leave you alone, but they

32
00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:46.480
refuse. They refuse to stop saying that Jesus has risen from the grave.

33
00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:51.420
In fact in Acts chapter 5 Peter stands up when they're being threatened and he

34
00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:53.280
speaks on behalf of the Apostles.

35
00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:57.900
He says we can't. We must obey God rather than men.

36
00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:03.380
Regardless of whether we accept some of the later grisly apocryphal accounts about

37
00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:07.840
the deaths of the apostles what we know for sure is that all the apostles were

38
00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:13.100
willing to suffer and die for their belief that jesus had conquered the grave

39
00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:19.100
and the fifth point is that there is good historical evidence that at least some

40
00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:24.780
of the apostles actually died as martyrs take james the brother of jesus

41
00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:29.860
for example there's an account from josephus a jewish writer at the end of the first

42
00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:35.640
century take James the brother of John there's an evidence a recording of his death

43
00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:41.400
in Acts 12:2 at the hands of Herod and there are multiple pieces of evidence

44
00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:46.100
different documents pointing out from the first and second century that both Peter

45
00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:51.760
and Paul died as martyrs and there is no evidence that any of the Apostles

46
00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:54.440
recanted their beliefs.

47
00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.580
Wait right here.

48
00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:02.020
You might be thinking, wait a minute.

49
00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:06.180
What about all the other people throughout history who've been willing to die for

50
00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:11.240
their beliefs? In fact, what about modern-day Muslim terrorists who died for their

51
00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:13.740
faith? Does that mean Islam is true?

52
00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:17.620
Yet here's an important distinction to keep in mind.

53
00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:23.220
They weren't eyewitnesses of Muhammad doing miracles or allegedly receiving the

54
00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:28.920
Quran. At best, they received their convictions fourth, fifth or sixth hand

55
00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:34.000
from somebody else. Their deaths provide no more evidence for the truth of Islam

56
00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.400
than my own death if I died as a martyr would provide evidence for Christianity.

57
00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:41.840
But the apostles were eyewitnesses.

58
00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:45.540
They saw the risen Jesus with their own eyes.

59
00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:50.380
So if we conclude that they made it up, we'd have to say that they died for

60
00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:52.860
something that they knew was false.

61
00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:55.400
and that's difficult to believe.

62
00:04:56.020 --> 00:05:01.560
This alone doesn't prove that Christianity is true, but it does show the depth of

63
00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:05.500
the sincerity of the Apostles. They weren't making this story up.

64
00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:08.600
They weren't liars. This wasn't a big conspiracy.

65
00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:14.480
They were willing to suffer and die for their belief that Jesus had risen from the

66
00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:14.720
grave.

67
00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:24.130
I wonder what else could the Apostles have done to convince us of the depth of

68
00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:26.130
the sincerity of their beliefs.

